## Weighted Mean and Custom Aggregates

A weighted mean multiplies each value by a weight, sums those products, then divides by the sum of weights. No `stats/weighted-mean` verb exists, so we build it with `map`, `apply`, and guards.

```scheme
;; Compute weighted mean of values with corresponding weights.
;; Returns weighted mean, or 'nan if lists are empty or mismatched length.
(define (weighted-mean values weights)
  (cond
   ((not (= (length values) (length weights)))
    'nan)
   ((null? values)
    'nan)
   (else
    (let ((weighted-sum (apply + (map * values weights)))
          (weight-total (apply + weights)))
      (if (= weight-total 0)
          'nan
          (/ weighted-sum weight-total))))))

(weighted-mean '(10 20 30) '(1 2 3))
;; => 23.333...  ;; (10*1 + 20*2 + 30*3) / (1+2+3) = 140/6

(weighted-mean '(5 10) '(0 0))
;; => nan  ;; zero total weight

(weighted-mean '(10 20) '(1 2 3))
;; => nan  ;; length mismatch
```

Guard for length match and zero total weight. Compute weighted sum with `(map * values weights)` then divide. This is a custom aggregate—no verb for it, but easy to compose.

