## Recursive Aggregation: Nested Sums

Sometimes you have nested lists (e.g., sales by region by month) and you want to sum at multiple levels. Here's a program that computes per-region totals and a grand total:

```scheme
;; Compute per-region totals and grand total from nested sales data.
;; Input: list of (region . sales-list) pairs.
;; Output: (list (region . total) ... (grand-total . sum-of-all))
(define (regional-totals data)
  (if (null? data)
      (list (cons 'grand-total 0))
      (let* ((region-totals (map (lambda (pair)
                                   (let ((region (car pair))
                                         (sales (cdr pair)))
                                     (cons region (apply + sales))))
                                 data))
             (grand (apply + (map cdr region-totals))))
        (append region-totals (list (cons 'grand-total grand))))))

