   (south . (8 9 10))
   (west . (20 22 25))))
;; => ((north . 37)
;;     (south . 27)
;;     (west . 67)
;;     (grand-total . 131))
```

Map over the data to compute per-region sums, then sum those sums for the grand total. This is *hierarchical aggregation*—a two-level fold.

