## Multi-Metric Dashboard Route

Bring it all together: a program that takes a series and returns a \"dashboard\" of stats—count, mean, stddev, min, max, p50, p95, and flags for any anomalies.

```scheme
;; Compute a full stats dashboard for a series.
;; Returns an alist with multiple metrics and an anomaly count.
(define (stats-dashboard series)
  (cond
   ((null? series)
    (list 'escalate \"empty-series\" \"cannot compute dashboard on empty list\"))
   ((< (length series) 3)
    (list 'escalate \"insufficient-data\" \"need at least 3 points for dashboard\"))
   (else
    (let* ((count (length series))
           (mean (apply / (list (apply + series) count)))
           (sq-diffs (map (lambda (x) (expt (- x mean) 2)) series))
           (variance (apply / (list (apply + sq-diffs) count)))
           (stddev (sqrt variance))
           (sorted (sort series <))
           (min-val (car sorted))
           (max-val (car (reverse sorted)))
           (p50 (percentile series 50))
           (p95 (percentile series 95))
           (zscores (if (= stddev 0)
                        (map (lambda (x) 0.0) series)
                        (map (lambda (x) (/ (- x mean) stddev)) series)))
           (anomalies (length (filter (lambda (z) (> (abs z) 2)) zscores))))
      (list (cons 'count count)
            (cons 'mean mean)
            (cons 'stddev stddev)
            (cons 'min min-val)
            (cons 'max max-val)
            (cons 'p50 p50)
            (cons 'p95 p95)
            (cons 'anomalies anomalies))))))

(stats-dashboard '(10 12 14 16 18 20 50))
;; => ((count . 7)
;;     (mean . 20.0)
;;     (stddev . 13.4...)
;;     (min . 10)
;;     (max . 50)
;;     (p50 . 16)
;;     (p95 . 50)
;;     (anomalies . 1))

(stats-dashboard '())
;; => (escalate \"empty-series\" ...)
```

This is the capstone route: twelve computed values, assembled into an alist. Guards at the top, honest escalation if the input is bad. Every stage uses only core Scheme or wired verbs. The result is a complete, actionable summary.

